Dear All,

1) I have a very long legend with 13 items and I would like to break it in two columns. I have found this:

guides(fill=guide_legend(ncol=2))
which doesn’t work and I am not sure what I am doing wrong.
 cols <- rainbow(13, s = 1, v = 1, start = 0, end = max(1, 13 - 1)/13, alpha = 1)
 label_s <- c("20km","50km","100km","5 Nearest Neigh.","10 Nearest Neigh.","15 Nearest Neigh.","Sphere of Influence","Gabriel Graph","Relative Graph","First Order Queen W","Second Order Queen W", "First Order Rook W","Second Order Rook W")
p <- ggplot(DF, aes(x=Year))+
  geom_line(aes(y=MoranI,colour=factor(order_plot),size=factor(order_plot)),linetype="dotted")+
  scale_size_manual(name="Contiguity",values = c(0.5,0.5,0.5,0.5,0.5,0.5,0.5,0.5,0.5,0.5,0.5,1.2,0.5),labels=label_select)+
  geom_line(aes(y=MoranI.sig,colour=factor(order_plot),size=factor(order_plot)),linetype=1)+
  labs(title = "", x = "", y = "") +
  scale_x_continuous(breaks=c(1981,1985,1990,1995,2000,2005,2011),limits=c(1981,1986))+
  scale_colour_manual(name = 'Contiguity', values = col,labels=label_select)+
  scale_fill_discrete(name="legendName")+
 theme(legend.position=c(0.85,0.22))+
 guides(fill = guide_legend(ncol=2,bycol=T))+
facet_wrap(~data.var,ncol=3)

2) I would like to create labels for my panels (obtained through facet_wrap, without modifying the original data frame. I have tried this options, which seems the quickest and most recyclable. One is to write a function and add it in my facet_wrap line: facet_wrap(~label_var,ncol=3,labeller=mf_labeller)
but it doesn’t work.
mf_labeller <- function(var, value){
   value <- as.character(value)
  if (var=="data.var") {
     value[value=="ASFR_15_all_1"] <- "15-19"
     value[value=="ASFR_20_all_1"]   <- "20-24"
     value[value=="ASFR_25_all_1"] <- "25-29"
   }
   return(value)
}

